            "block_id": "b-1a6b40bb71eb66a082e841d5",
            "quote": "The History department allows students great latitude in creating a course of study that reflects their interests and career objectives. At the lower-division level (1000/2000) students must complete a total of 12 credit hours, including one survey series (1110/20, 1150/60, 1170/80, 2255/56), AND two other courses from the following list: 1105, 1110-1120, 1150-1160, 1170-1180, 1190, 2110, 2130, 2255-2256. At the upper division level (300/400), students must complete at least 24 credit hours, including HIST 491 (Historiography) and HIST 492 (Senior Seminar)."
          }
        ]
